{"id": "EUVD-2026-103741", "enisaUuid": "0204a1da-827c-3994-be0b-06f83951a095", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nHID: alps: fix use-after-free on input2 registration failure\n\nalps_input_configured() stores data->input2 before calling\ninput_register_device().  If registration fails, input_free_device()\nfrees the input device but data->input2 still points to the freed memory.\nalps_input_configured() calls hid_hw_open() before allocating input2, so\nURBs are already active and raw_event can fire during the failure window.\nA U1_SP_ABSOLUTE_REPORT_ID report arriving then causes u1_raw_event()\nto dereference the freed data->input2 -> use-after-free.\n\nFix by only storing input2 into drvdata after successful registration\nand adding a NULL guard in the raw_event path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:16:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:20:40", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/64f824dccfd316fd3db8ea1cc4e8a76ad6a02740", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2e55d76e6e8a756f6d87c241de975599f82b02fa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ef8ca5bb4c8b9696f38b1bebce1c851baa02b77b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a8ad63158165bacd6a1d7420e0fe5364c913b06", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47e5e177e9e4e10da6f2759d5ce8d049e33efdc4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/925da1d2a24787f24872de13a4680437c54de179", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/443f6b93442b10b972a16f57ceaaea75b77892b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d3aba3442798ce4a4c8ce3104d7b286d61e605f9"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98501", "GHSA-56g2-px47-cfcj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00ecba31-5afa-3ffd-9c4c-61fe58091272", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "216bc0ba-c5e9-3252-9e77-7f19d302987a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2562756dde550901c224e3805102bdfc17e7d13a <5a8ad63158165bacd6a1d7420e